+REGIME: WHICH FORWARD PRODUCED THE POSITION (2026-09-03, tessera#102)
+---------------------------------------------------------------------
+``dump`` has always scored **prompt positions**: ``max_tokens: 1`` with
+``prompt_logprobs: K`` over a 512-token prompt, so every scored position comes
+out of one 512-row prefill forward.  Any serving lane that only runs at small
+M is therefore invisible to the number: a GEMV kernel with a max batch of 8
+never executes on a scored forward, and a two-arm A/B over such a kernel
+returns a *bit-identical* null -- clean, precise, and evidence about the
+prefill path only.  That is worse than no instrument, because a null reads
+like a strong positive result.
+
+``--regime decode`` is the second, opt-in mode.  It feeds each chunk's prefix
+incrementally with vLLM's prefix cache on, so every scored position is an
+**M = 1** forward:
+
+* one warm-up request per chunk over the whole chunk fills the prefix cache
+  (that request IS a prefill, and is the only prefill the regime performs);
+* then one request per scored position, ``prompt = chunk[:L]`` with
+  ``(L - 1) % stride == 0``, ``max_tokens: 1`` and ``logprobs: K``, so the
+  serve computes exactly ONE new row and samples from it;
+* ``stride`` must equal the serve's KV block size (16 by default), because the
+  prefix cache hits on whole blocks only;
+* the M = 1 claim is ENFORCED, not asserted: the serve's own
+  ``usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens`` must account for every prompt
+  token but one, on every scored request, or the dump refuses.  That field
+  requires ``--enable-prompt-tokens-details`` on the serve, so a serve without
+  it produces no dump rather than an unverified one.
+
+It is a **NEW METRIC**, not a better one: the same corpus and the same
+conditioning, a stride-subsample of the prefill regime's positions, and a
+different executed kernel.  Prefill-regime and decode-regime numbers are
+therefore not comparable, ``compare`` refuses a cross-regime pair outright
+(no ``--allow-mismatch`` escape), and the regime rides inside the metric
+identity that gets pasted next to the number.
+
 SERVING SURFACES
 ----------------
