+#: vLLM's prefix cache hits on WHOLE KV blocks, so a request whose prefix is
+#: not block-aligned recomputes the tail of its last block -- up to
+#: ``block_size`` rows, which is exactly the regime the decode mode exists to
+#: avoid.  The stride is therefore the serve's KV block size, not a taste:
+#: 16 is vLLM's default and the minimum FlashAttention accepts.  A wrong value
+#: is caught per request by the cached-token check, not carried silently.
+DECODE_STRIDE_DEFAULT = 16
+
