+#: unless the request asks for ids (``return_tokens_as_token_ids``), and token
+#: text is lossy: two ids can decode to one string and non-UTF8 byte pieces
+#: come back as replacement characters.  The decode regime therefore requires
+#: id keys and refuses anything else, rather than building a plausible wrong
+#: distribution out of text.
+DECODE_TOKEN_ID_KEY = re.compile(r"^token_id:(\d+)$")
